{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 25,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These also are proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is the glory of God to conceal a thing;\nBut the glory of kings is to search out a matter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the heavens for height, and the earth for depth,\nSo the heart of kings is unsearchable.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take away the dross from the silver,\nAnd there cometh forth a vessel for the refiner:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take away the wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the king,\nAnd his throne shall be established in righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put not thyself forward in the presence of the king,\nAnd stand not in the place of great men:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For better is it that it be said unto thee, Come up hither,\nThan that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince,\nWhom thine eyes have seen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go not forth hastily to strive,Lest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou know not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " what to do in the end thereof,\nWhen thy neighbor hath put thee to shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Debate thy cause with thy neighbor ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",And disclose not the secret of another;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lest he that heareth it revile thee,\nAnd thine infamy turn not away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A word fitly spoken\nIs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " apples of gold in network of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an ear-ring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "So is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wise reprover upon an obedient ear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the cold of snow in the time of harvest,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "So is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a faithful messenger to them that send him;\nFor he refresheth the soul of his masters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " clouds and wind without rain,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "So is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that boasteth himself of his gifts falsely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By long forbearing is a ruler persuaded,\nAnd a soft tongue breaketh the bone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee,\nLest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy foot be seldom in thy neighbor’s house,\nLest he be weary of thee, and hate thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man that beareth false witness against his neighbor\nIs a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble\nIs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one that taketh off a garment in cold weather, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vinegar upon soda,\nSo is he that singeth songs to a heavy heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat;\nAnd if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou wilt heap coals of fire upon his head,\nAnd Jehovah will reward thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The north wind bringeth forth rain;\nSo doth a backbiting tongue an angry countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop,\nThan with a contentious woman in a wide house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cold waters to a thirsty soul,\nSo is good news from a far country.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a troubled fountain, and a corrupted spring,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "So is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a righteous man that giveth way before the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is not good to eat much honey;So ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to search out their own glory is grievous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.25.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.25.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He whose spirit is without restraint\nIs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a city that is broken down and without walls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
